### [2026-07-30 03:21:55] CONTINUITY

Design ruling for TASK C, from the source (stable-audio-3/models/transformer.py): differential to_qkv = Linear(dim, dim*5), chunk ORDER [q, k, v, q_diff, k_diff] (line 766); non-differential = dim*3 [q,k,v]; cross-attn to_kv = 2 blocks [k,v]. So NOT a 3-way split — the GENERAL rule that covers all cases: split the fused projection's ROWS into out_features//dim equal blocks of dim rows each, orthogonalize each block separately. The semantic labels don't matter to NS5 — what matters is each functional projection getting its own spectral treatment; equal-dim row-blocks achieves that for 5-way, 3-way, and 2-way without special-casing. IMPORTANT adapter nuance (the campaign arms train dora-rows r128, not fullft): the spectral params are lora_A (r x in) and lora_B (out x r). The split applies to lora_B of fused modules (5dim x r -> five dim x r blocks) — its rows ARE the per-projection up-projections. lora_A is input-side/shared across the 5 outputs — unsplittable, leave whole. dora magnitude is a row-vector, scalar-group anyway. So: row-block rule on lora_B + (if fullft ever uses it) on W itself; skip lora_A. Zach's own caveat applies — he doesn't Muon LoRAs at all — which is exactly why arm 4 is an empirical test, not a correctness fix. --C

