- Sec 5: the 5.6-7.4x cosine distance is Muon FULL fine-tuning on Math/Code only (PDF, weight-distance paragraph); under LoRA it REVERSES (Muon 0.2-0.8x of Adam), and on Commonsense (mild mismatch) Muon moves less even in full FT (0.65-0.75x). Added. Also added: the paper's Muon is the Moonlight variant (update pre-rescaled to Adam size, Appendix B), so its lrs are already in Adam-like units. Checked OK: 78%/39% gap shrink, rank claim (LoRA-Muon wins at low-moderate rank, degrades at high), cosine decay + 3% warmup.
